From 82172c58f12cf1ffaf9facccfa79243ebcbb7eb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:22:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: the field Psynergy menu, and tools for building
 screens

The field Psynergy menu crashed the desktop build: it stores through two
sprites that are not there (the marker MenuCursor_Create's comment
describes, and the Psynergy cursor before it is made), which the
cartridge's BIOS takes. Natively the marker is a sprite no window
carries, and the cursor's store is skipped until it exists.

For building and checking screens without walking to them:
--screen NAME (or TBS_SCREEN) and the headless script's "screen NAME"
open a screen straight from the field (native_dev.c: classviewer,
mechanics), through a request the field loop takes
(gNativeScreenRequest). The headless build now runs a script's "reset" by
starting itself again at the next command, with the save on disk, as the
mGBA driver resets the console.

The GBA ROM is byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8ykfbWFo924wEqysLhg
