+
+### Tools for building screens
+
+- `--screen NAME` (or `TBS_SCREEN=NAME`) opens a screen straight from the
+  field once the scene has faded in, and the headless script command
+  `screen NAME` opens it then: `classviewer` (the scholar's, for Isaac),
+  `mechanics` (the mechanics guide). `native_dev.c` lists them; the field loop
+  takes the request (`gNativeScreenRequest`, `field_sequence_run.c`).
+- The headless build runs a script's `reset` (as the mGBA driver does): it
+  starts itself again with `--resume N` at the command after the reset, with
+  the save on disk, so `save_continue.txt` works.
